<title>FRANCE: France says supports gene-food labelling.</title>
<headline>France says supports gene-food labelling.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French farm minister Philippe Vasseur said Wednesday he supported labelling food products containing gene-altered crops to ease consumer concern over their safety.</p>
<p>&quot;We must impose labelling because otherwise consumers will lose confidence. This is crucial. Consumers have the right to know what they are buying,&quot; Vasseur told the annual meeting of the CGB sugar beet planters federation.</p>
</text>
